# Template for the real manifest.
#
# Copy to ~/.dotfiles-local/backup.manifest (NOT into the repo) and edit.
# One path per line. `#` starts a comment. `~` and $VARS are expanded.
# Missing paths are warned and skipped, not fatal.
#
# Recommended (single canonical tree — see README § Secrets layout):
#
~/.secrets
#
# ~/.secrets/ layout (all vault-backed, never in git):
#
#   ~/.secrets/
#   ├── env.sh                          # sourced by zsh (API keys, exports)
#   ├── ssh/                            # → ~/.ssh/* via symlinks.tsv
#   ├── config/
#   │   ├── gh/hosts.yml                # → ~/.config/gh/hosts.yml
#   │   └── moltbook/credentials.json   # → ~/.config/moltbook/credentials.json
#   └── apps/
#       ├── raycast/                    # manual .rayconfig / export bundles
#       └── transmit/                   # manual .transmitservers exports
#
# Shottr license prefs: add a manifest line for the sandbox plist path if you
# vault-back it directly (see restore-apps.sh comment), or restore from a
# dated snapshot after mounting the vault.
#
# Monokai Pro (Sublime): license file is NOT in the repo — keep under:
#   ~/.secrets/apps/sublime-text/Theme - Monokai Pro.sublime-settings
# Covered by the ~/.secrets line above when using the recommended manifest.
#
# Canary Mail: make backup-canary → ~/.secrets/apps/canary-mail/ (realms + plist).
# Also covered by ~/.secrets when using the recommended manifest.
#
# Migrating from an old manifest that listed ~/.config/* or ~/.ssh/* paths?
# Move files into the ~/.secrets/ tree above, then `make link`.
